@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Program slicing — backward_slice(&cpg, seed, max_nodes)
start
:worklist = {seed}
visited = {};
while (worklist non-empty AND size(visited) < max_nodes ?) is (yes)
  :pop n
add n to visited;<<#E5DBFF>>
  :push PDG predecessors of n
(ControlDependence + DataDependence,
followed in reverse);<<#E5DBFF>>
endwhile (no)
:return visited (bounded slice);<<#FFE3E3>>
stop
note right
  <b>forward_slice</b> is the same BFS over
  PDG <i>successors</i> (outgoing ControlDependence
  + DataDependence). Both filter on
  <latex>e.kind.is\_pdg()</latex> and stop once
  <latex>|visited| = max\_nodes</latex>.
end note
legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#E5DBFF>| PDG BFS step |
  |<#FFE3E3>| bounded result |
endlegend
@enduml
